{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Its shoots.</b> Long branches — called ווידי״ץ בְּלַעַז." "<b>And it was as though budding.</b> Resembles budding — and 'as though budding': it seemed to me in my dream as though it was budding. After the blossom a bud emerged, and tendrils formed — אשפנ״יר בְּלַעַז — and afterward they ripened. And it is as the Targum renders of פּוֹרַחַת: a large blossom from a flower, as it is written ״וּבֹסֶר גֹמֵל יִהְיֶה נִצָּה״ (Isaiah 18), and written ״וַיֹּצֵא פֶרַח, וַהֲדַר וַיָּצֵץ צִיץ״ (Numbers 17)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French gadier or similar, 'shoot/cane'", 1 "the la'az אשפנ״יר is Old French espamir/esplent, 'tendril/young shoot'; the phrase והיא כפורחת נץ גדול מפרח appears to cite Onkelos or Targum; ע״כַ is an abbreviation, read here as עַל כֵּן, 'therefore'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:51.228465664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}